In article <1992Mar3.053439.14724@usenet.ins.cwru.edu> jwk3@po.CWRU.Edu (John W. Kale) writes:
>
>	Arghhhh! Once again, my character has just been killed after
>losing all of its good weapons and armor to nymphs. (There were three
>of those awful things running around this time...) Is there any way
>to defend onself against them? Besides running away, maybe...?
>					-John

find a nice large room.  With pickaxe (mug a dwarf if necessary) dig a
pit in front of each of the doors, or somewhere on the path that the nymph
would have to take to reach you in the center from the door.  Then sit in
the center, doing a 5. repeatedly.  The nymph will come back, fall in the
pit and hopefully be stuck for a while.  Peg away at the nymph withe your
daggers, arrows, rocks, or whatever until she is deade.  Of course you will
fall in your pit when you recover your possessions, but oh well.

if you find yourself face to face with a nymph in a corridor, and it's your
move, you can make her go away by applying a mirror in her direction, which
she will steal instead of anything else.


